[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3775920534","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113886#issuecomment-3775920534","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113886","id":3775920534,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hD_mW","user":{"login":"tylerbobik","id":9973218,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NzMyMTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9973218?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerbobik","html_url":"https://github.com/tylerbobik","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerbobik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerbobik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerbobik/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerbobik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerbobik/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerbobik/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerbobik/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerbobik/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerbobik/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-21T03:07:07Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T03:07:07Z","body":"Testing this on a Surface with Fedora 42. The touch seems to stop working after the first touch event is triggered.\r\n\r\nI have had a few times where after the first touch it will highlight buttons when touched, but most of the time touch just seems to stop working. The app doesn't die though, if I bring in a mouse, I can press buttons and everything still.\r\n\r\nThis is with a .NET build as well, if that would effect anything.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3775920534/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3875813704","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113886#issuecomment-3875813704","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113886","id":3875813704,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nBDlI","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T07:23:58Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T07:24:48Z","body":"Hi @TheShed412, thank you for testing! I finally had a change to take a stab at this and found a solution. It looks like mutter does not return a `wl_touch.frame` event after `wl_touch.up`. I can kinda see why they did that as the protocol says \"no further events will be sent for this touch point\") but that's somewhat unfortunate IMO.\r\n\r\nEdit: while I was at it I also rebased the branch.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3875813704/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performe